<p>New in v7, <code>verify()</code> also upgrades a hash it finds out of date — hashed under a weaker cost or an older
algorithm than the class declares. Verify against a <code>$2y$04$</code> hash while the class asks for cost 12 and the
stored hash comes out <code>$2y$12$</code>, so a password store migrates itself as people log in.</p>
<p>The third argument turns that off. Pass <code>false</code> when the record is not yours to save, or when you would
rather batch the writes, and <code>verify()</code> records what it found instead of acting on it:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">if (</span><span class="text-var">$user</span><span class="text-kw">-&gt;</span><span class="text-var">verify</span><span class="text-kw">(</span><span class="text-str">&#039;password&#039;</span><span class="text-kw">, </span><span class="text-var">$attemptedPassword</span><span class="text-kw">, </span><span class="text-var">false</span><span class="text-kw">)) {
    if (</span><span class="text-var">$user</span><span class="text-kw">-&gt;</span><span class="text-var">needsRehash</span><span class="text-kw">()) {
        </span><span class="text-var">$user</span><span class="text-kw">-&gt;</span><span class="text-var">rehash</span><span class="text-kw">(</span><span class="text-str">&#039;password&#039;</span><span class="text-kw">, </span><span class="text-var">$attemptedPassword</span><span class="text-kw">);
    }
}
</span></code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>needsRehash()</code> reports the outdated hash and <code>rehash()</code> acts on it, re-encoding under the current
<code>$hashAlgorithm</code> and <code>$hashOptions</code> and saving. With the default it has already run by the time <code>verify()</code>
returns.</p>
<p><code>rehash()</code>'s value argument carries <code>#[\SensitiveParameter]</code>, so PHP redacts it from stack traces.</p>
